WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.440 --> 00:00:08.520
A yarn balance or scale
is a useful tool to identify the yards per

2
00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:15.320
pound of yarn, maybe mistery
yarn or a skein of yarn.

3
00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:19.880
By knowing the yards per pound,
you can more easily compare the weights

4
00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:26.160
of yarn, this tool is available from many
sources specializing in weaving yarn.

5
00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:31.800
They're available for weighing,
yarn in both metric and imperial units.

6
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:35.320
Set up, the scale on a level surface.

7
00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:40.480
Set the metal pins into the slots
on each side of the box.

8
00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:44.000
Now cut a strand of yarn and hang it over

9
00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:49.840
the notched edge of the scale
with the yarn hanging freely.

10
00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:56.400
Initially, the scale will hang downward
from the weight of the yarn.

11
00:00:56.600 --> 00:01:02.560
Use a pair of scissors and carefully start
trimming both ends of the yarn strand

12
00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:09.960
in about half-inch increments
until the scale is level.

13
00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:24.440
Remove the strand of yarn and then measure
it, just stretch it just slightly.

14
00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:30.960
And multiply the inch measurement by 100
to determine the yards per pound.

15
00:01:31.160 --> 00:01:37.320
In this example, it measures 9.5 inches times 100

16
00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:43.640
this yarn and would be approximately
950 per pound.

17
00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:45.480
Now, here's another tip

18
00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:50.000
to determine the amount of yarn remaining
on a cone or a ball of yarn,

19
00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:55.720
weigh the cone on a kitchen or
postal scale, a digital scale,

20
00:01:55.920 --> 00:02:00.040
subtract about an ounce
for the paper cone.

21
00:02:00.880 --> 00:02:04.080
Divide by 16, the yards per pound,

22
00:02:04.280 --> 00:02:10.240
determined by the yard balance,
16 ounces equals one pound.

23
00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:12.400
To find the number of yards remaining,

24
00:02:12.600 --> 00:02:17.400
multiply the answer by the number
of ounces of yarn remaining.

25
00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:20.040
Here's an example,
using the yarn balance,

26
00:02:20.230 --> 00:02:23.880
we determined that this yarn is
approximately 950 yards

27
00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:32.720
per pound.950 divided by 16
equals 59 yards per ounce.

28
00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:38.040
The remaining yarn weighs
6.5 ounces.

29
00:02:38.240 --> 00:02:41.240
Do the math and this little ball has about

30
00:02:41.440 --> 00:02:43.760
383
yards remaining.

